WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.810 --> 00:00:03.119
If a cryptocurrency like Bitcoin

00:00:03.120 --> 00:00:05.099
were to become a commonly accepted

00:00:05.100 --> 00:00:07.259
medium of exchange, a global,

00:00:07.260 --> 00:00:09.149
decentralized monetary system that

00:00:09.150 --> 00:00:11.879
no third party can stop or control,

00:00:11.880 --> 00:00:13.349
would the U.S. government attempt to

00:00:13.350 --> 00:00:15.509
make it illegal and to prosecute

00:00:15.510 --> 00:00:17.129
the developers who contribute to its

00:00:17.130 --> 00:00:18.689
code base?

00:00:18.690 --> 00:00:20.369
Is software protected by the First

00:00:20.370 --> 00:00:21.449
Amendment?

00:00:21.450 --> 00:00:22.529
Will the government one day

00:00:22.530 --> 00:00:24.209
prosecute individuals who designed

00:00:24.210 --> 00:00:26.099
3D printed guns and then make their

00:00:26.100 --> 00:00:28.169
plans downloadable on the Internet?

00:00:28.170 --> 00:00:30.359
Last week brought cause for alarm

00:00:30.360 --> 00:00:31.949
that a federal crackdown on the

00:00:31.950 --> 00:00:34.079
decentralized open source software

00:00:34.080 --> 00:00:36.359
movement might be coming.

00:00:36.360 --> 00:00:38.009
In the past, the US government has

00:00:38.010 --> 00:00:39.959
pursued financial service companies

00:00:39.960 --> 00:00:41.939
like cryptocurrency exchanges,

00:00:41.940 --> 00:00:43.829
holding them criminally liable for

00:00:43.830 --> 00:00:45.659
mishandling other people's money

00:00:45.660 --> 00:00:47.519
or first facilitating international

00:00:47.520 --> 00:00:49.169
payments without following know your

00:00:49.170 --> 00:00:51.209
customer and other regulations.

00:00:51.210 --> 00:00:53.189
But what happened on August 8th was

00:00:53.190 --> 00:00:54.149
different.

00:00:54.150 --> 00:00:55.529
The U.S. Treasury Department

00:00:55.530 --> 00:00:57.449
announced it was adding tornado

00:00:57.450 --> 00:00:59.129
cash, a tool for making

00:00:59.130 --> 00:01:00.419
cryptocurrency transactions

00:01:00.420 --> 00:01:02.069
anonymous to the U.S.

00:01:02.070 --> 00:01:03.599
sanctions list.

00:01:03.600 --> 00:01:05.039
Dutch authorities arrested a

00:01:05.040 --> 00:01:07.349
suspected developer of tornado cash,

00:01:07.350 --> 00:01:09.239
accusing him of facilitating

00:01:09.240 --> 00:01:11.069
laundering of billions of dollars

00:01:11.070 --> 00:01:12.269
of stolen funds.

00:01:12.270 --> 00:01:14.129
What's he guilty of?

00:01:14.130 --> 00:01:16.319
Writing code and making it free

00:01:16.320 --> 00:01:17.969
on the Internet?

00:01:17.970 --> 00:01:19.079
What triggered the U.S.

00:01:19.080 --> 00:01:20.939
crackdowns on tornado cash was the

00:01:20.940 --> 00:01:22.139
allegation that the Hacking

00:01:22.140 --> 00:01:24.089
Collective, the Lazarus Group,

00:01:24.090 --> 00:01:25.919
used tornado cash in

00:01:25.920 --> 00:01:27.149
an attempt to disguise

00:01:27.150 --> 00:01:28.919
cryptocurrency payments worth about

00:01:28.920 --> 00:01:31.289
$455 million

00:01:31.290 --> 00:01:33.389
to North Korea's missile program.

00:01:33.390 --> 00:01:35.039
The Treasury Department's action is

00:01:35.040 --> 00:01:36.599
reminiscent of the case against the

00:01:36.600 --> 00:01:38.999
software developer Phil Zimmermann,

00:01:39.000 --> 00:01:40.589
who developed and distributed

00:01:40.590 --> 00:01:42.989
software known as P-Gp

00:01:42.990 --> 00:01:44.909
in the early 1990s, which

00:01:44.910 --> 00:01:46.889
was the first widely accessible

00:01:46.890 --> 00:01:48.629
tool for sending messages over the

00:01:48.630 --> 00:01:50.699
Internet with powerful encryption.

00:01:50.700 --> 00:01:52.499
I'm delighted to hear good stories

00:01:52.500 --> 00:01:54.959
about how it's used in places where

00:01:54.960 --> 00:01:57.059
there are oppressive governments.

00:01:57.060 --> 00:01:58.589
Zimmerman became the target of a

00:01:58.590 --> 00:02:00.419
three year federal investigation on

00:02:00.420 --> 00:02:02.219
the grounds that the software was so

00:02:02.220 --> 00:02:04.319
powerful that making it possible

00:02:04.320 --> 00:02:06.779
for foreigners to download it online

00:02:06.780 --> 00:02:08.939
was the equivalent of distributing

00:02:08.940 --> 00:02:10.769
weapons to foreign countries without

00:02:10.770 --> 00:02:11.729
permission from the State

00:02:11.730 --> 00:02:12.629
Department.

00:02:12.630 --> 00:02:14.159
The government ultimately dropped

00:02:14.160 --> 00:02:15.989
the investigation, thanks in part to

00:02:15.990 --> 00:02:18.179
free speech activists who printed

00:02:18.180 --> 00:02:20.369
the entire PGB source code in a book

00:02:20.370 --> 00:02:22.199
published by MIT Press

00:02:22.200 --> 00:02:24.029
and sold it abroad, to make

00:02:24.030 --> 00:02:25.949
the point that its creation was

00:02:25.950 --> 00:02:27.869
a form of writing protected by

00:02:27.870 --> 00:02:29.849
the First Amendment just like any

00:02:29.850 --> 00:02:30.850
other book.

00:02:31.420 --> 00:02:33.309
Zimmerman's legal battle was part of

00:02:33.310 --> 00:02:35.739
what's known as the crypto wars,

00:02:35.740 --> 00:02:37.539
which refers to the ongoing battle

00:02:37.540 --> 00:02:40.209
to keep powerful cryptography legal.

00:02:40.210 --> 00:02:42.189
We just want to make sure we have a

00:02:42.190 --> 00:02:44.079
trapdoor and a key under

00:02:44.080 --> 00:02:45.999
some judge's authority where

00:02:46.000 --> 00:02:48.069
we can get there if somebody

00:02:48.070 --> 00:02:49.659
is planning a crime.

00:02:49.660 --> 00:02:51.579
Sanctioning of tornado cash

00:02:51.580 --> 00:02:52.959
is the latest chapter in that

00:02:52.960 --> 00:02:54.879
struggle to better understand its

00:02:54.880 --> 00:02:56.259
implications.

00:02:56.260 --> 00:02:57.699
I reached out to attorney Jerry

00:02:57.700 --> 00:03:00.159
Brito, who's the executive director

00:03:00.160 --> 00:03:02.409
of COIN Center, a nonprofit focused

00:03:02.410 --> 00:03:04.629
on policy issues and regulations

00:03:04.630 --> 00:03:05.949
facing Bitcoin and other

00:03:05.950 --> 00:03:07.659
cryptocurrencies.

00:03:07.660 --> 00:03:09.549
Briefly, what is tornado

00:03:09.550 --> 00:03:11.439
cash and what action did the

00:03:11.440 --> 00:03:13.389
U.S. Treasury just take against it?

00:03:14.780 --> 00:03:15.780
So

00:03:16.700 --> 00:03:18.579
looks like such an easy question.

00:03:18.580 --> 00:03:19.899
What's been sanctioned here is not a

00:03:19.900 --> 00:03:21.009
person.

00:03:21.010 --> 00:03:22.809
There's a sanction on a tool.

00:03:22.810 --> 00:03:25.089
And so the sanction really is on

00:03:25.090 --> 00:03:26.619
millions of Americans who otherwise

00:03:26.620 --> 00:03:28.029
might want to use that tool for

00:03:28.030 --> 00:03:29.919
completely lawful purposes

00:03:29.920 --> 00:03:32.019
as a result of this sanctioning,

00:03:32.020 --> 00:03:34.209
the developers of the tool

00:03:34.210 --> 00:03:35.769
have had their accounts suspended at

00:03:35.770 --> 00:03:37.959
GitHub, where they publish code.

00:03:37.960 --> 00:03:39.579
That in itself is not a violation of

00:03:39.580 --> 00:03:40.449
the First Amendment because that's a

00:03:40.450 --> 00:03:42.399
private company basically saying,

00:03:42.400 --> 00:03:43.569
we don't want you to be publishing

00:03:43.570 --> 00:03:45.699
on our platform, but it is

00:03:45.700 --> 00:03:47.559
indicia of a chilling effect on

00:03:47.560 --> 00:03:48.339
free speech.

00:03:48.340 --> 00:03:50.169
So basically, anybody who is

00:03:50.170 --> 00:03:51.459
in any way associated with this

00:03:51.460 --> 00:03:53.349
tool, which again is a neutral tool

00:03:53.350 --> 00:03:55.179
that can be used for good

00:03:55.180 --> 00:03:57.069
or for ill, these people are

00:03:57.070 --> 00:03:59.409
now being basically

00:03:59.410 --> 00:04:01.359
deplatformed in such a way that they

00:04:01.360 --> 00:04:02.709
don't have an ability to speak and

00:04:02.710 --> 00:04:04.659
may in the future not choose

00:04:04.660 --> 00:04:05.979
to speak because of the

00:04:05.980 --> 00:04:06.980
repercussions of these sanctions.

00:04:08.020 --> 00:04:09.729
Tornado cash is what's known as a

00:04:09.730 --> 00:04:11.319
coin mixer, meaning it blends

00:04:11.320 --> 00:04:12.669
together multiple cryptocurrency

00:04:12.670 --> 00:04:14.589
transactions and then breaks them

00:04:14.590 --> 00:04:16.389
out again with the purpose of making

00:04:16.390 --> 00:04:18.069
it harder for sleuths to follow the

00:04:18.070 --> 00:04:19.059
payment trail.

00:04:19.060 --> 00:04:20.379
It's a technique for protecting

00:04:20.380 --> 00:04:22.239
financial privacy and has been used

00:04:22.240 --> 00:04:23.979
to avoid detection by authoritarian

00:04:23.980 --> 00:04:25.089
governments.

00:04:25.090 --> 00:04:26.679
Last month I put out a video in

00:04:26.680 --> 00:04:28.479
which I asked Alex Gladstein of the

00:04:28.480 --> 00:04:30.069
Human Rights Foundation if he was

00:04:30.070 --> 00:04:31.719
worried that the government was on

00:04:31.720 --> 00:04:33.519
the verge of banning coin mixers

00:04:33.520 --> 00:04:34.089
outright.

00:04:34.090 --> 00:04:35.619
Is that something you're worried

00:04:35.620 --> 00:04:37.659
about, that the very act

00:04:37.660 --> 00:04:39.489
of anonymizing your bitcoin will be

00:04:39.490 --> 00:04:41.469
deemed by governments to be money

00:04:41.470 --> 00:04:41.989
laundering?

00:04:41.990 --> 00:04:43.749
What is legally protected as open

00:04:43.750 --> 00:04:45.429
source software and free speech is

00:04:45.430 --> 00:04:47.949
is coinjoins because they are merely

00:04:47.950 --> 00:04:48.969
their open source code.

00:04:48.970 --> 00:04:50.439
There's no no one taking control of

00:04:50.440 --> 00:04:51.429
your bitcoin.

00:04:51.430 --> 00:04:53.319
It's a collaborative spend that's

00:04:53.320 --> 00:04:54.320
completely legal here.

00:04:55.360 --> 00:04:56.829
And I think if someone tried to make

00:04:56.830 --> 00:04:58.059
it illegal, there'd would be very,

00:04:58.060 --> 00:05:00.129
very strong, you know, push back

00:05:00.130 --> 00:05:01.809
on all kinds of, you know, First

00:05:01.810 --> 00:05:03.909
Amendment and Third Amendment,

00:05:03.910 --> 00:05:05.319
etc., like all kinds of different

00:05:05.320 --> 00:05:06.669
grounds.

00:05:06.670 --> 00:05:08.529
So I think that collaborative

00:05:08.530 --> 00:05:10.299
spending is going to be defended in

00:05:10.300 --> 00:05:11.949
the United States, certainly not in

00:05:11.950 --> 00:05:12.729
a dictatorship.

00:05:12.730 --> 00:05:13.569
But but here.

00:05:13.570 --> 00:05:14.049
Yes.

00:05:14.050 --> 00:05:16.179
One reason that Americans

00:05:16.180 --> 00:05:18.909
might want to use this tool is to

00:05:18.910 --> 00:05:20.739
make anonymous

00:05:20.740 --> 00:05:23.199
political speech contributions.

00:05:23.200 --> 00:05:25.059
Vitalik Buterin, who is one of

00:05:25.060 --> 00:05:26.769
the creators of Ethereum, used

00:05:26.770 --> 00:05:28.659
tornado cash to donate funds

00:05:28.660 --> 00:05:30.189
to Ukraine.

00:05:30.190 --> 00:05:31.149
That's another reason.

00:05:31.150 --> 00:05:32.259
You know, there are many political

00:05:32.260 --> 00:05:34.299
reasons why you might want to use

00:05:34.300 --> 00:05:35.300
tornado cash. That's completely
legitimate.

00:05:36.830 --> 00:05:38.449
In the 1990s, the intelligence

00:05:38.450 --> 00:05:39.829
community sought congressional

00:05:39.830 --> 00:05:41.509
authority to outlaw end to end

00:05:41.510 --> 00:05:42.979
encryption on the grounds that

00:05:42.980 --> 00:05:44.329
terrorists could use it to

00:05:44.330 --> 00:05:45.979
communicate without the NSA

00:05:45.980 --> 00:05:46.849
listening in.

00:05:46.850 --> 00:05:48.769
Similarly, when adding tornado cash

00:05:48.770 --> 00:05:50.719
to the sanctions list, the Treasury

00:05:50.720 --> 00:05:52.879
Department asserted that all virtual

00:05:52.880 --> 00:05:54.139
currency mixers that assist

00:05:54.140 --> 00:05:56.359
criminals are a threat to national

00:05:56.360 --> 00:05:57.379
security.

00:05:57.380 --> 00:05:58.909
Treasury will continue to

00:05:58.910 --> 00:06:00.739
investigate the use of mixers for

00:06:00.740 --> 00:06:02.509
illicit purposes.

00:06:02.510 --> 00:06:04.279
People who look at the broad strokes

00:06:04.280 --> 00:06:06.439
here might say, 'You know what?

00:06:06.440 --> 00:06:08.209
North Korea's using this to launder

00:06:08.210 --> 00:06:10.009
hundreds of millions of dollars of

00:06:10.010 --> 00:06:11.929
stolen money to build weapons that

00:06:11.930 --> 00:06:13.009
threaten us.

00:06:13.010 --> 00:06:15.079
Something has to be done.' What

00:06:15.080 --> 00:06:16.080
do you say to that?

00:06:16.970 --> 00:06:18.799
Yeah, you know,

00:06:18.800 --> 00:06:20.809
I'm very sympathetic to

00:06:20.810 --> 00:06:22.699
the folks in the national

00:06:22.700 --> 00:06:24.589
security community

00:06:24.590 --> 00:06:26.509
who are seeing this thing that

00:06:26.510 --> 00:06:28.339
is a tool is being used

00:06:28.340 --> 00:06:30.349
by North Koreans to launder funds

00:06:30.350 --> 00:06:31.399
that potentially could then be used

00:06:31.400 --> 00:06:32.569
to build weapons of mass destruction,

00:06:32.570 --> 00:06:33.570
etc..

00:06:34.490 --> 00:06:35.989
And they want to do something about

00:06:35.990 --> 00:06:36.990
this.

00:06:37.250 --> 00:06:39.619
And unfortunately,

00:06:39.620 --> 00:06:41.599
where we are is that the only thing

00:06:41.600 --> 00:06:43.939
that seems to be available to them

00:06:43.940 --> 00:06:45.739
would be to make it so that nobody

00:06:45.740 --> 00:06:46.579
can use it. Right.

00:06:46.580 --> 00:06:47.899
Because it really is because it's a

00:06:47.900 --> 00:06:50.839
decentralized, unowned

00:06:50.840 --> 00:06:52.759
application that anybody can

00:06:52.760 --> 00:06:54.979
use. There's really no good way

00:06:54.980 --> 00:06:57.379
to be able to allow

00:06:57.380 --> 00:06:59.359
law abiding citizens to use it and

00:06:59.360 --> 00:07:01.399
disallow bad actors from

00:07:01.400 --> 00:07:03.109
using it. Basically, it's a tool

00:07:03.110 --> 00:07:04.669
like email, like the Internet too,

00:07:04.670 --> 00:07:06.709
that is available for anybody

00:07:06.710 --> 00:07:07.729
to use.

00:07:07.730 --> 00:07:09.049
And so then really, it comes down to

00:07:09.050 --> 00:07:10.279
a question of equities, right?

00:07:10.280 --> 00:07:12.229
What do you think is

00:07:12.230 --> 00:07:13.849
more important?

00:07:13.850 --> 00:07:15.889
Is it a risk of

00:07:15.890 --> 00:07:17.749
bad guys using it,

00:07:17.750 --> 00:07:18.750
or is it

00:07:19.790 --> 00:07:21.439
more important to you that law

00:07:21.440 --> 00:07:23.209
abiding citizens have first and

00:07:23.210 --> 00:07:24.859
Fourth Amendment rights and privacy

00:07:24.860 --> 00:07:26.419
and free speech rights and the

00:07:26.420 --> 00:07:27.470
ability to protect them?

00:07:29.060 --> 00:07:30.109
Zimmerman says the Treasury
Department's

00:07:30.110 --> 00:07:32.269
action is a threat to the entire

00:07:32.270 --> 00:07:34.189
cryptocurrency space because it

00:07:34.190 --> 00:07:36.019
also made it illegal for any

00:07:36.020 --> 00:07:38.029
U.S. citizen to hold cryptocurrency

00:07:38.030 --> 00:07:39.799
that previously ran through the

00:07:39.800 --> 00:07:41.569
Tornado Cash Mixer.

00:07:41.570 --> 00:07:42.859
That's like making it against the

00:07:42.860 --> 00:07:44.749
law to possess $100 bill that

00:07:44.750 --> 00:07:45.949
at some point passed through the

00:07:45.950 --> 00:07:47.749
hands of someone who did something

00:07:47.750 --> 00:07:48.739
illegal.

00:07:48.740 --> 00:07:50.239
Even if you have no knowledge of its

00:07:50.240 --> 00:07:51.379
provenance.

00:07:51.380 --> 00:07:53.239
One researcher found that almost

00:07:53.240 --> 00:07:54.769
half the addresses in the Ethereum

00:07:54.770 --> 00:07:56.569
network are two degrees of

00:07:56.570 --> 00:07:58.489
separation away from a tornado cash

00:07:58.490 --> 00:07:59.449
transaction.

00:07:59.450 --> 00:08:01.219
In other words, they received a

00:08:01.220 --> 00:08:02.869
payment from an address that has

00:08:02.870 --> 00:08:04.369
received a payment that ran through

00:08:04.370 --> 00:08:05.389
the mixer.

00:08:05.390 --> 00:08:06.799
What if somebody sends you money

00:08:06.800 --> 00:08:08.509
through tornado cash that you never

00:08:08.510 --> 00:08:10.009
solicited or know nothing about?

00:08:10.010 --> 00:08:11.599
This is the way blockchains work.

00:08:11.600 --> 00:08:13.409
And so we've seen that this week.

00:08:13.410 --> 00:08:14.299
There's somebody has been doing

00:08:14.300 --> 00:08:16.579
that, has been sending small amounts

00:08:16.580 --> 00:08:18.529
of cryptocurrency using

00:08:18.530 --> 00:08:21.349
tornado cash to prominent

00:08:21.350 --> 00:08:22.429
celebrity addresses.

00:08:22.430 --> 00:08:24.409
So Jimmy Fallon, for example, was

00:08:24.410 --> 00:08:26.569
sent crypto through tornado

00:08:26.570 --> 00:08:28.039
cash after the sanctions.

00:08:28.040 --> 00:08:29.239
And so now technically, he is in

00:08:29.240 --> 00:08:30.769
violation of sanctions law.

00:08:30.770 --> 00:08:32.479
What do people like that do?

00:08:32.480 --> 00:08:34.908
And then imagine

00:08:34.909 --> 00:08:37.249
that you are somebody who receives

00:08:37.250 --> 00:08:38.719
through a just normal, law abiding

00:08:38.720 --> 00:08:39.859
transaction with somebody who, you

00:08:39.860 --> 00:08:41.329
know, is a law abiding person.

00:08:41.330 --> 00:08:42.678
You receive funds, but then you

00:08:42.679 --> 00:08:44.058
notice that the funds that you

00:08:44.059 --> 00:08:46.159
received, maybe four

00:08:46.160 --> 00:08:48.199
or five persons back

00:08:48.200 --> 00:08:50.599
went through tornado cash.

00:08:50.600 --> 00:08:52.519
What is your obligation there, if

00:08:52.520 --> 00:08:53.809
any? I would think that would be

00:08:53.810 --> 00:08:54.739
none.

00:08:54.740 --> 00:08:56.809
But OFAC has not been clear about

00:08:56.810 --> 00:08:57.689
what that would be.

00:08:57.690 --> 00:08:58.939
They said nothing. It was clear is

00:08:58.940 --> 00:09:00.199
not is not the right word if they've

00:09:00.200 --> 00:09:01.579
been silent. If this president

00:09:01.580 --> 00:09:04.129
stands, there's no reason why

00:09:04.130 --> 00:09:06.379
OFAC couldn't say that

00:09:06.380 --> 00:09:07.380
signal.

00:09:07.970 --> 00:09:09.649
The chat app that's encrypted is

00:09:09.650 --> 00:09:11.959
used by North Koreans to facilitate

00:09:11.960 --> 00:09:13.519
that activity and it is therefore

00:09:13.520 --> 00:09:16.039
banned. Signal is a firm

00:09:16.040 --> 00:09:16.879
and so you could put it on a

00:09:16.880 --> 00:09:18.619
sanctions list. Now, I kind of take

00:09:18.620 --> 00:09:19.939
that back maybe just a little bit

00:09:19.940 --> 00:09:20.929
because signal happens to be an

00:09:20.930 --> 00:09:22.549
American company and you can't

00:09:22.550 --> 00:09:23.389
sanction Americans.

00:09:23.390 --> 00:09:24.289
You would have to go through some

00:09:24.290 --> 00:09:25.099
due process.

00:09:25.100 --> 00:09:26.100
Right.

00:09:26.960 --> 00:09:28.789
But you can imagine

00:09:28.790 --> 00:09:30.709
that this could happen to some

00:09:30.710 --> 00:09:31.669
open source code.

00:09:31.670 --> 00:09:34.009
Right. So there is open source code

00:09:34.010 --> 00:09:35.959
that if you run it, you can

00:09:35.960 --> 00:09:38.899
have a signal like decentralized

00:09:38.900 --> 00:09:40.579
encrypted chat.

00:09:40.580 --> 00:09:42.529
Well, potentially that could be

00:09:42.530 --> 00:09:43.459
added to the list.

00:09:43.460 --> 00:09:45.709
And so it's not just cryptocurrency,

00:09:45.710 --> 00:09:47.689
right? It's anything that is just

00:09:47.690 --> 00:09:48.499
code.

00:09:48.500 --> 00:09:51.109
Where do you see

00:09:51.110 --> 00:09:52.639
this fight going?

00:09:52.640 --> 00:09:54.079
I think what's happening here is

00:09:54.080 --> 00:09:56.479
that regulators

00:09:56.480 --> 00:09:58.309
and law enforcement have

00:09:58.310 --> 00:10:01.309
always relied on intermediaries

00:10:01.310 --> 00:10:03.229
to be able to catch bad guys.

00:10:03.230 --> 00:10:04.339
Right. So they can always go to

00:10:04.340 --> 00:10:06.139
intermediary chokepoints, whether

00:10:06.140 --> 00:10:07.849
it's in communications or financial

00:10:07.850 --> 00:10:09.589
transactions, and they can go to

00:10:09.590 --> 00:10:10.579
those intermediaries.

00:10:10.580 --> 00:10:13.129
And using legal process

00:10:13.130 --> 00:10:15.109
and regulation, they can

00:10:15.110 --> 00:10:16.699
fluctuate their ends.

00:10:16.700 --> 00:10:18.349
And with crypto technology, what

00:10:18.350 --> 00:10:19.489
they're finding is a lot of the

00:10:19.490 --> 00:10:21.259
things that you needed to use an

00:10:21.260 --> 00:10:23.089
intermediary for you no longer

00:10:23.090 --> 00:10:24.019
do. These things are being

00:10:24.020 --> 00:10:25.249
disintermediated.

00:10:25.250 --> 00:10:27.139
And so when they go to

00:10:27.140 --> 00:10:28.729
try to serve legal process on an

00:10:28.730 --> 00:10:29.597
intermediary, they find it, wait

00:10:29.598 --> 00:10:31.279
there's no intermediary here.

00:10:31.280 --> 00:10:32.280
Right. There's

00:10:33.110 --> 00:10:34.309
there's there's a mixing service.

00:10:34.310 --> 00:10:35.309
But the mixing service isn't a

00:10:35.310 --> 00:10:37.159
service is not a

00:10:37.160 --> 00:10:38.689
company.

00:10:38.690 --> 00:10:40.279
And so I think this is where they're

00:10:40.280 --> 00:10:42.379
taking actions that

00:10:42.380 --> 00:10:45.109
are unprecedented and probably

00:10:45.110 --> 00:10:46.549
maybe they don't realize it or

00:10:46.550 --> 00:10:49.159
probably are straying

00:10:49.160 --> 00:10:50.569
into violations of constitutional

00:10:50.570 --> 00:10:51.570
rights.

00:10:52.340 --> 00:10:53.449
And so that's just something we're

00:10:53.450 --> 00:10:54.589
going to have to go through.

00:10:54.590 --> 00:10:56.119
At the end of the day, I'm

00:10:56.120 --> 00:10:58.369
optimistic because our Constitution

00:10:58.370 --> 00:11:00.349
has served us well for 250 years.

00:11:00.350 --> 00:11:01.969
I think it will continue to do so,

00:11:01.970 --> 00:11:03.799
and I think we will find the right

00:11:03.800 --> 00:11:05.569
balance. Unfortunately, I think it's

00:11:05.570 --> 00:11:06.409
going to have to go through the

00:11:06.410 --> 00:11:07.729
courts.

00:11:07.730 --> 00:11:10.039
Tornado cash is a tool

00:11:10.040 --> 00:11:11.929
and tools are neutral, just

00:11:11.930 --> 00:11:14.269
like Bitcoin encryption, guns,

00:11:14.270 --> 00:11:15.499
even telephones.

00:11:15.500 --> 00:11:17.119
Terrorists and dictators can use

00:11:17.120 --> 00:11:19.159
them, as can human rights activists

00:11:19.160 --> 00:11:20.179
and dissidents.

00:11:20.180 --> 00:11:21.379
The government should target the

00:11:21.380 --> 00:11:23.359
criminals and authoritarians who

00:11:23.360 --> 00:11:25.189
threaten human freedom, not

00:11:25.190 --> 00:11:27.259
the programmers and cryptographers

00:11:27.260 --> 00:11:29.119
who build new technologies that

00:11:29.120 --> 00:11:31.009
can better secure human freedom.

